# wallpapers-chan — AI Rules

Source of truth: `.ai/` (read before planning or coding).

## Stack (match existing code)

- Next.js App Router under `src/app/`
- React client components (`"use client"`) + Tailwind
- API routes in `src/app/api/**/route.js`
- Mongoose models in `src/lib/models/`; Better Auth users via `src/lib/users.js`
- Client HTTP: `src/lib/apiRequest.js` (axios, credentials)
- Images: `src/components/Image/Image.jsx` + `src/lib/mediaUrls.js`

## Mandatory agent behavior

1. Before coding: read `.ai/workflows/before-coding.md` and relevant `.ai/rules/*`
2. Prefer editing existing files; do not invent APIs, env vars, models, or routes
3. Search for existing helpers before adding new utils
4. Minimal diff — no drive-by refactors
5. After changes: self-review with `.ai/workflows/code-review.md` + matching checklist
6. Repo conventions win when they conflict with `.ai` (document exceptions)

## Required reading by task

| Task | Read |
|------|------|
| Any change | `.ai/README.md`, `rules/coding.md`, `rules/architecture.md` |
| UI / pages / components | `rules/react.md`, `rules/frontend.md`, `checklists/frontend-checklist.md` |
| API / auth / DB | `rules/api.md`, `rules/backend.md`, `rules/database.md`, `rules/security.md` |
| Stuck / bugs | `workflows/debugging.md`, `prompts/debugger.md` |

## Non-goals for agents

- Do not rewrite the app to Clean Architecture layers unless asked
- Do not add TypeScript unless asked (project is mostly JS)
- Do not introduce a second styling system (Tailwind + existing tokens only)
